{
 "format": "ids",
 "version": 1,
 "about": "The four ids (deliverable, evaluation, invoice line, settlement), the four verdicts and the rule that bills a deliverable once (src/knos/ids.py, src/knos/ledger.py `billed_once`; docs/METER.md, One deliverable is billed once). An id is its prefix (dlv, evl, inv, stl), an underscore and the first 24 hex characters of sha256(\"knos.id.v1\" || 0x00 || kind || 0x00 || for each part: its length in bytes as u32 big-endian, then its UTF-8 bytes); the kinds are deliverable, evaluation, invoice_line, settlement; a number is a part as its decimal text. ids.deliverable(scope, key); ids.evaluation(deliverable, artifact, policy, evaluator, run); ids.invoice_line(supplier, invoice, line); ids.settlement(deliverable, method, reference). ids.kind_of: the kind of an id, or null. ids.expect: the id when it is of the kind named, refused otherwise. ids.order_scope: an order as 64 lowercase hex characters, from that or from its base58 address of 32 to 44 characters. ids.verdict: the verdict a loose word means (case, spaces and hyphens do not matter; passed and clean mean accepted, failed and refused rejected, unverified, pending and none insufficient_evidence). ids.billed_once: the places, from 0, of the evaluations billed as outcomes: the first accepted of each deliverable.",
